Chapter: DeskLeadingMetricsTest
  cites Works chapter GopFat16
  cites Works chapter GopFont
  cites Works chapter GopDraw
  cites Works chapter GopDesk
  cites Works chapter GopComposite
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 ShellRefinement recorded the desk's paragraph leading as a HYPOTHESIS from a
 photograph: too much leading, cause guessed as a line step computed from
 `comp-glyph-h`. The step was `dk-line-h`, a fixed 18 scaled by the desk
 scale, consulting the face never. This prints the face's own metrics beside
 it so the gap is a number rather than an adjective. Measured 2026-08-21 that
 step was 36 against a face cell of 41, so it was TIGHTER than the face and
 the fix as recorded would have loosened it; at ppem 16 the same constant was
 36 against a cell of 21, half again too loose. One constant, wrong in both
 directions, which is what `dk-line-step` reading `gf-gh` replaced.

 WHAT THE GATED RUN PROVES IS NOT THE LEADING. `seed/Codex.img` carries no
 typeface on purpose, and the battery attaches no disk here, so the recorded
 answer is the no-volume line: it proves this chapter still compiles against
 `GopFont` and `GopDraw` and that the mount is reached, and NOTHING about
 type. The table lives in `ShellRefinement.md` with the command that rebuilds
 it, which needs an image built by `build-boot-img.ps1`. Do not read a green
 here as the leading being settled (L-NAMED).

 The ppem is the one `desk-font` loads at, `dk-ui-ppem w`, and the width is
 the desk's default. Reading them off the same expressions the desk uses is
 the point: a constant copied here would measure this chapter.

  dlm-w : Integer = 1600

 Stage 9.5 asks for SMALL type, and "small" is an adjective until the face has
 been asked what each ppem actually costs in rows (L-ADJECTIVE). The sweep
 answers the only three numbers a layout cares about, per ppem: the cell the
 rasterizer produces, the ascent, and the cap height, which is what a reader
 perceives as the size of the type. It also prints the width of one string, so
 a ppem that is unusably narrow shows up as an advance and not as a look.

  dlm-pad : Text, Integer -> Text
  dlm-pad (t) (n) = if text-length t >= n then t else dlm-pad (t & " ") n

  dlm-row : GopFont, Integer -> Text
  dlm-row (f) (ppem) =
    dlm-pad ("ppem " & integer-to-text ppem) 10
    & dlm-pad ("cell " & integer-to-text (f.gf-gh)) 10
    & dlm-pad ("asc " & integer-to-text (f.gf-asc)) 9
    & dlm-pad ("cap " & integer-to-text (f.gf-cap)) 9
    & "CODEX wide " & integer-to-text (gfont-text-w f "CODEX")

  dlm-sweep : Fat16Volume, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Console, Device.Port] Integer
  dlm-sweep (vol) (ppems) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then i
    else act
      f <- gfont-load vol "CMUNSS.TTF" (list-at ppems i)
      r <- if f.gf-ok == False
        then print-line-uni ("ppem " & integer-to-text (list-at ppems i) & ": not loaded")
        else print-line-uni (dlm-row f (list-at ppems i))
      dlm-sweep vol ppems (i + 1) n
    end

  opening : [Console, Device.Port] Nothing = act
    m <- gfat-mount-esp
    if m.gm-ok == False then print-line-uni "no FAT volume on the boot medium"
    else act
      let ppem = dk-ui-ppem dlm-w
      in let s = ui-scale dlm-w
      in act
        f <- gfont-load (m.gm-vol) "CMUNSS.TTF" ppem
        if f.gf-ok == False then print-line-uni "CMUNSS.TTF: not loaded"
        else act
          print-line-uni ("ppem requested        : " & integer-to-text ppem)
          print-line-uni ("desk scale s          : " & integer-to-text s)
          print-line-uni ("face cell gf-gh       : " & integer-to-text (f.gf-gh))
          print-line-uni ("face ascent gf-asc    : " & integer-to-text (f.gf-asc))
          print-line-uni ("face cap gf-cap       : " & integer-to-text (f.gf-cap))
          print-line-uni ("step dk-line-step     : " & integer-to-text (dk-line-step f s))
          print-line-uni ("bitmap step 18 * s    : " & integer-to-text (dk-line-h * s))
          print-line-uni ("step minus face cell  : " & integer-to-text (dk-line-step f s - f.gf-gh))
          print-line-uni "ppem sweep:"
          q <- dlm-sweep (m.gm-vol) [10, 12, 14, 16, 18, 20, 24, 32] 0 8
          print-line-uni ("sweep rows            : " & integer-to-text q)
        end
      end
    end
  end
